{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment3.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: run `flutter pub get` explicitly, like both sibling web-build jobs**

The two existing web builds both resolve dependencies explicitly before building:

- `pages.yml` — "Example app pub get" step (`flutter pub get` in `flutter_app`), then build;
- `ci.yml` `build-web` — `cd flutter_app && flutter pub get`, then build.

This job goes straight to `flutter build web --release --base-href /app/`. The flutter tool auto-resolves when the package config is missing/outdated, so it will almost certainly work — but since this PR's stated goal is "same build shape as Pages", mirroring the explicit step costs nothing and keeps the three web jobs on one pattern (and immune to any future change in the tool's implicit pub-get behavior).
"}

{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment5.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: link the doc from the README/site so it's discoverable**

Nothing links to `docs/web-rehosting.md` today (checked README and `site/`). Issue #1100 allowed "docs/web-rehosting.md **or README section**" — the file exists, but a user who just downloaded `fa-web-spa.zip` from a release page has no path to it. A one-line pointer from README (and/or the site download section) closes the loop; the release asset description could reference it too.
"}

